Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
define
    omSay code={
        v := tell(argument);
        m := *v["matched"]; c := *v["consumed"];
        cerr "OMDRIVE " argument " matched= " m " consumed= " c:;
        };
    omOne code={
        r := Grokking[argument];
        x := *r["rightBrace"];
        modsOf(*x);
        };
    omTwo code={
        r := OmMod[argument];
        x := *r["OmA"];
        modsOf(*x);
        };
    ;
register(OmMod);
define
    OmA    isRule ka-="a";
    OmP    isRule OmA% kp-="p";
    OmQ    isRule OmA& kq-="q";
    OmU    isRule OmA_ ku-="u";
    OmN    isRule OmA kn-="n";
    ;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities OmMod list;
cerr "OM-1 rightBrace: three references, one shared body":;
omOne("SetBrackets");
omOne("Braced");
cerr "OM-2 OmA referenced four ways":;
omTwo("OmP");
omTwo("OmQ");
omTwo("OmU");
omTwo("OmN");
cerr "OM-3 the scratch rules still parse":;
omSay("OmP ap");
omSay("OmQ aq");
omSay("OmU au");
omSay("OmN an");
omSay("OmN xn");
cerr "OMMODT SENTINEL":;
stop();

omModT -- OBJECT MODEL STROKE 1: A MATCH MODIFIER IS A FACT ABOUT ONE REFERENCE, NOT ABOUT THE RULE.

Before stroke 1, modify() wrote `_` `{ }` (unGuarded), `%` (isPercent) and `&` (isPointer) onto the
BODY, which every reference to a rule shares with the rule itself. So SetBrackets' `rightBrace}` put
unGuarded on the body Braced and Limit also read, and `OmA%` in OmP marks OmA's body for every rule
that names OmA. After stroke 1 the fact lands on the reference's own rStuff (modUnGuarded, modPercent,
modPointer) and the body keeps only its own meanings.

OM-1  modsOf on rightBrace in SetBrackets and Braced (Limit, the third reference, was retired 2026-09-28). isUnGuarded is the predicate the guard test
      itself calls (instance, then rule), so the row reads what the parser reads.
      want: SetBrackets 1 (declared `}`), Braced 0.
OM-2  OmA referenced with % & _ and plain, then OmA itself.
      want: each fact on its own reference's instance bits, none on the body; OmN and OmA read 0.
OM-3  the scratch rules drive and match as before (values pinned both sides of the stroke).
